# Template: Front-End Basic

## File Purpose and Relationship

This file provides a basic template for front-end component requirements in the PolygonExpress project. It focuses solely on giving structure to the initial requirements.md file for simple front-end components.

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

This file is a Manual rule type and should be referenced as a project-rule-parameter in the plan-mode message-command:

```
plan-mode: front-end-workflow @parameters/front-end/plan-mode/template-basic.mdc
```

## Requirements Template

When this template is applied, it will create the following structure in requirements.md:

```markdown
# Component Requirements

## Objective
[What is the purpose of this component?]

## Component Functionality
[What should this component do?]

## Props/Interface
[What props or interface should this component accept?]

- [Prop 1]: [Description]
- [Prop 2]: [Description]
- [Prop 3]: [Description]

## Visual Requirements
[What should this component look like?]

## State Management
[What state does this component need to manage?]

## Dependencies
[What other components or libraries does this component depend on?]

## Success Criteria
[How will we know this component is implemented correctly?]
```

## Template Application

When the template is applied, I will:
1. Create or update requirements.md with this template
2. Leave all sections empty for completion
3. Wait for the requirements to be completed before proceeding with any planning

## Next Steps
1. Complete the requirements template with component details
2. Once requirements are complete, proceed with planning the implementation approach

## Use Cases
- Simple UI components
- Presentational components
- Form elements
- Navigation items
- Layout components
- Simple interactive elements 